2. Third-party components
-------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The distributed binary statically links Go modules and embeds the compiled
frontend (web/embed.go does //go:embed dist), so it redistributes third-party
code.

The complete list - every component with its detected license and its copyright
line - is in THIRD-PARTY-NOTICES.txt. That file is GENERATED by reading the
LICENSE file each component actually ships with; it is not typed by hand, and
the BSD / ISC license texts are reproduced there in full because those licenses
require the notice to travel with the binary. Do not edit it by hand.

